#### Note 1 ####
Word correspondences must contain at least one bookmark to be saved
#### End Note 1 ####

#### Note 2 ####
-- To open pluggable DB
ALTER PLUGGABLE DATABASE ALL OPEN;
ALTER PLUGGABLE DATABASE ALL SAVE STATE;
#### End Note 2 ####

####  Note 3 ####
In oracle there is the root DB on a domain orcl.server.vm
and the pluggable one which is used in client connecitons 
localhost:1521/orcl_PDB.server.vm
tablespaces represents the DB name, however in connections with clients we use the username in the DB name feild
Root DB & pluggable DB (Created with the wizard) -> tablespaces with users
Root -> pluggable -> tablespace -> users

for connection with any client: use existing -> create
#### End Note 3 ####

#### Note 4 ####
Altering queries can only be performed on the root DB not the pluggable
#### End Note 4 ####

#### Note 5 ####
--Creating table space and user with permissions

CREATE TABLESPACE Tarasol
DATAFILE 'Tarasol.dbf' 
SIZE 100M 
AUTOEXTEND ON NEXT 50M 
MAXSIZE UNLIMITED;

-- Create the user 
create user zaher
  identified by "123"
  default tablespace Tarasol
  temporary tablespace TEMP;


grant connect to zaher;
grant resource to zaher;
grant create trigger to zaher;
grant create view to zaher;
grant unlimited tablespace to zaher;
grant execute on CTXSYS.Ctx_Ddl to zaher;
GRANT CREATE MATERIALIZED VIEW TO zaher;
#### End Note 5 ####

#### Note 5 ####
To use the mobile app, 
1- Install middleware
2- Activate from IAM
3- From original settings folder copy Resources and themes into the folder mobile files
4- In appsettings.json edit the ip for Tarasol api, and set verison to 0
5- In tarasol.config add the url for IAM
#### End Note 5 ####

#### Note 6 ####
Archmate connection with Tarasol
1- Token from admin user into the file AMWK10 -> settings -> settings.config
2- Set ip in the identityserver settings in AMWI10 | AMAdmin10 | AMWK10
3- Connection settings -> stores -> create new permenant store from ArcMate type, and set the token and Service url (AMService10 url without slash)
4- Connection settings -> Archive settings -> enable Archive integration
5- Search in archive url => AMWK10 url
6- Archive Service url   => AMService10 url (API)
7- From unites and positions settings -> edit unit settings -> Folder path => Folder created in AMWI10 

#### End Note 6 ####

#### Note 7 ####
On mobile app: 
1- You can't stamp, only sign from saved or free sign.
2- You can't move in the repeated stage.
3- You can't sent it back if you're not the owner (in repeated stages).
4- Only Archives from the server appears (Not Archmate's).
4- Approving shows an error but operation is successfull.
#### End Note 7 ####

#### Note 8 ####
--> To recycle all application pools: 

& "$env:windir\system32\inetsrv\appcmd.exe" list apppool /state:Started /xml | & "$env:windir\system32\inetsrv\appcmd.exe" recycle apppool /in

--> After adding the bin path to Paht variable:
 & appcmd list apppool /state:Started /xml | & appcmd recycle apppool /in
#### End Note 8 ####

#### Note 9 ####
-->To list Oracle services:

Get-Service -Name "Oracle*" |
    Format-Table Name, DisplayName, Status, StartType -AutoSize

--> Start Oracle services: 

    Get-Service -Name "Oracle*" |
        Where-Object Status -ne "Running" |
        Start-Service


-->To find the directory of a Service

Get-CimInstance Win32_Service |
    Where-Object { $_.Name -like "Oracle*" } |
    Select-Object Name, State, PathName
#### End Note 9 ####
